---
layout: layouts/base.njk
tags: pages
title: "The Seven Steps: A Free Self-Care Practice | Reem Glasco"
description: Walk through the seven steps of Effort-less Self-Care with a breathing guide, two short timers and journal prompts that save privately in your own browser.
nav: The Practice
order: 9.6
priority: 0.7
bodyClass: practice
script: /assets/js/practice.js
---
<section class="shell band">
  <p class="eyebrow">Free, and nothing to sign up for</p>
  <h1>The seven steps</h1>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>This is the whole practice from <a href="/book/">Effort-less Self-Care</a>, free to use
    here. It takes a few minutes. There is nothing to fix and no way to do it wrong: you sit,
    you notice what your body is doing, and you write down what you find, or you do not.
    Anything you type <strong>stays in this browser on this device</strong> and is never sent
    anywhere, including to Reem.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cta-row" data-practice-start hidden>
    <button class="cta" type="button" data-action="begin">Begin today's practice</button>
    <a class="cta cta--quiet" href="#reflections">See what I have written</a>
  </div>
  <p class="note" data-practice-nojs>All seven steps are laid out below. Turn on JavaScript for
  the guided version, with the breathing guide, the timers and saved answers.</p>
</section>

<nav class="practice-dots" aria-label="Progress through the seven steps" data-practice-dots hidden></nav>

{%- for s in site.steps %}
<section class="shell band practice-step{% if loop.index0 % 2 == 1 %} practice-step--alt{% endif %}"
         id="step-{{ s.n }}" data-step="{{ loop.index0 }}" data-key="{{ s.key }}">
  <div class="split split--aside">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Step {{ s.n }} of 7</p>
      <h2>{{ s.title }}</h2>
      <p class="step-card__quote">&ldquo;{{ s.quote }}&rdquo;</p>
      <div class="step-instr">
        <p>{{ s.instruction }}</p>
        {%- if s.breathing %}
        <p class="say"><em>Inhale:</em> &ldquo;I know I am breathing in fresh air.&rdquo;<br>
        <em>Exhale:</em> &ldquo;I know I am breathing out stress.&rdquo;</p>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>

      {%- if s.breathing %}
      <div class="breathe" data-breathe hidden>
        <div class="breathe__circle" data-breathe-circle>breathe</div>
        <p class="breathe__label" data-breathe-label>Three slow rounds, at your own pace.</p>
        <button class="cta cta--quiet" type="button" data-action="breathe">Start breathing, three rounds</button>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}

      {%- if s.timer %}
      <div class="timer" data-timer="{{ s.timer }}" hidden>
        <p class="timer__num" data-timer-num>{{ s.timer }}</p>
        <button class="cta cta--quiet" type="button" data-action="timer">Sit for {{ s.timer }} seconds</button>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}

      {%- if s.emotions %}
      <fieldset class="emotions" data-emotions hidden>
        <legend>If one of these fits, choose it. If none does, leave it.</legend>
        <button class="emotion" type="button" data-emotion="sad">Sad</button>
        <button class="emotion" type="button" data-emotion="angry">Angry</button>
        <button class="emotion" type="button" data-emotion="calm">Calm</button>
        <button class="emotion" type="button" data-emotion="happy">Happy</button>
      </fieldset>
      {%- endif %}

      {%- for prompt in s.prompts %}
      <p class="prompt">
        <label for="{{ s.key }}-{{ loop.index }}">{{ prompt }}</label>
        <textarea id="{{ s.key }}-{{ loop.index }}" rows="3"
          data-field="{{ s.key }}_{{ loop.index }}"
          placeholder="Write freely, or leave it blank. Getting stuck is fine."></textarea>
      </p>
      {%- endfor %}

      <p class="saved-hint" data-saved aria-live="polite"></p>

      <div class="cta-row" data-practice-nav hidden>
        <button class="cta cta--quiet" type="button" data-action="prev">Previous</button>
        <button class="cta" type="button" data-action="next">{% if s.n == 7 %}Finish{% else %}Continue{% endif %}</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <img class="step-art" src="{{ s.img }}" width="{{ s.w }}" height="{{ s.h }}" alt="{{ s.alt }}"
       loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endfor %}

<section class="band band--night" id="closing" data-closing hidden>
  <div class="shell split split--aside">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Final reflection</p>
      <h2>Just breathe</h2>
      <p>You sat back and observed your inner and outer world, not to fix or analyse it, but
      simply to notice it. Your breath is always with you: your silent guide.</p>
      <p class="quote-band">&ldquo;You are learning to listen.&rdquo;</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="cta" href="#reflections">Read what I wrote</a>
        <button class="cta cta--quiet" type="button" data-action="restart">Start again</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <img class="step-art" src="/assets/img/book-closing.jpg" width="760" height="760"
       loading="lazy" decoding="async"
       alt="Watercolour of sunrise through trees, warm light spreading across a green landscape.">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band" id="reflections">
  <h2>Your reflections</h2>
  <p>Everything you type is stored only in this browser, on this device, using its local
  storage. It never reaches a server, so it is private, and so it disappears if you clear your
  browsing data or switch devices. Copy anything you want to keep.</p>
  <div data-reflections>
    <p class="note">Nothing saved yet. Anything you write above appears here.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cta-row" data-reflections-actions hidden>
    <button class="cta cta--quiet" type="button" data-action="copy">Copy today's reflections</button>
    <button class="cta cta--quiet" type="button" data-action="clear">Delete everything saved</button>
  </div>
  <p class="saved-hint" data-copy-hint aria-live="polite"></p>
</section>

<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about the practice</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>Where do my answers go?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Nowhere. They are saved in your browser's local storage on this device and never
      transmitted. Reem cannot see them, this site has no analytics, and there is no account to
      create. The trade-off is that clearing your browsing data deletes them.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do I have to answer every prompt?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. Blank is a legitimate answer and getting stuck is part of it. The prompts exist to
      give attention somewhere to land, not to be completed.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How often should I do this?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Daily if it helps, weekly if that is more realistic, or only when you need to reset.
      The practice is short on purpose so that doing it is easier than deciding whether to.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What if something difficult comes up?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Stop, and come back to step three: hand on your chest, noticing your breath without
      changing it. This is a noticing practice, not trauma processing, and it is not a crisis
      resource. If what surfaced needs more than a page, that is worth taking to a therapist.
      <a href="/contact/">A consult here is free and fifteen minutes.</a></p>
    </div>
  </details>
  {% include "partials/crisis-note.njk" %}
</section>

{% include "partials/cta-band.njk" %}
